                "When Manu pulled his net back up, it was filled with glowing points of light. Lina gasped loudly, and Manu turned toward her hiding place. Instead of being angry, he smiled and invited her to come closer.",
                "What Lina saw amazed her. The net wasn't filled with stars from the sky, but with bioluminescent plankton from the ocean. The tiny creatures glowed with blue-green light, looking exactly like captured stars in the dark net.",
                "Manu explained that these microscopic organisms were just as magical as real stars. They lit up when disturbed, creating beautiful patterns in the water. For centuries, fishermen in their village had used this phenomenon to find their way home on dark nights.",
