                "The two families met in the spring, exactly as the old letters promised. They brought photos, stories, and warm bread. Amira put the letters back in the drawer, but this time she left the last page open, where a new address had been written. Since that day, every spring brings a phone call and a long <span class='mark'>conversation</span>."
